WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.680
A24 was the studio that brought us my favorite
horror film of 2017, It Comes At Night, and

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.040
judging from what people have been saying
about this movie at Sundance, it sounds like

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.020
their new film, Hereditary, could be another
success.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.700
Yesterday we got a trailer for it and it does
look promising.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.770
Look closer however and you'll see some downright
creepy details and things that just don't

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.960
add up... seemingly on purpose...

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.730
If you want to hear the one consistency I
did find, then make sure to stick around to

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.390
the end of this video.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.329
This is Things You Missed.

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:35.300
Let's just start at the beginning of the trailer.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.260
It opens on this miniature model of the house.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.420
It appears to be the house that they live
in which shows up about midway through the

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.420
trailer.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.961
This piece sitting on the chair should end
up going right here on the front of the house.

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:46.690
The garage doors are the same for both.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.780
And the front entrance and the overall shape
of the house seem consistent.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.579
But then you notice this window is missing
from the model and the colors are changed

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:58.430
entirely -- the model has beige wood and green
frames while the house is brown with dark

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.430
brown frames.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:03.910
In another shot we can also confirm that the
real house is missing this section too.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.729
Now it could just be that she's using the
miniature to plan to a remodel or something,

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:12.049
or she's an architect, as evidenced by these
blueprints, that reuses the same design elements

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:15.499
in many of her works, such as the garage door
and the front door.

00:01:15.499 --> 00:01:19.229
But what makes me think otherwise is that
there are other inconsistencies in the trailer

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:20.780
begging to be noticed.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.740
The treehouse is missing from the model altogether,
and because the treehouse looks like a small,

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.110
separate house house, you have to wonder if
she just sees it as another one of her creations.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.290
Just a crazy guess here because we don't know
a whole lot about this movie yet, but maybe

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.979
the mother starts to break down later in the
movie and loses sight of the difference between

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:38.560
her real family and the figurines.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.959
One more thing from this opening shot before
we move on.

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:43.719
There are two creepy photos pinned up in the
corner of the room.

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:47.310
I'm not sure what the first one is, but please
let me know your thoughts in the comments.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.889
But the second one looks like a pair of feet
standing in an overexposed doorway.

00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:54.600
If you're not convinced let me crank up the
contrast for you.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.459
Now let's look at this shot later in the trailer
where the Mom finds the figurine of her deceased

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:01.369
mother standing in the doorway.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:02.789
Connection?

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.909
Not definite.

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:06.240
But absolutely a possibility.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.170
Here's another inconsistency.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.730
Outside of the immediate family, which is
these guys, none of the people at the burial

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.030
are the same people who attend the service.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.860
See how there are a bunch of bearded guys
at the service?

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.159
None at the burial.

00:02:18.159 --> 00:02:20.100
See these bald guys at the burial?

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.400
Not at the service.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.950
The burial has four kids.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.560
The only kid at the service is the daughter.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.739
As far as I can tell, the immediate family
are the only ones to attend both events.

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:34.030
The mother even comments, "it's heartening
to see so many strange new faces here today.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.530
I know my mom would be very touched."

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:37.879
What does that even mean?

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:41.320
Why would you want strangers at your mother's
funeral?

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.790
Like I said, something doesn't add up.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.519
But it gets weirder...

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:49.989
The daughter is drawing a picture of her mother
hysterical and crying at the podium.

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:52.030
But we see at the podium, the mom is fine.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.780
It's at the burial that she's hysterical.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.129
Also, on the other page, what is this?

00:02:56.129 --> 00:02:57.680
This is terrifying!

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.489
If these drawings turn out to be telling of
things to come, then this is going to be one

00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:01.890
freaky scene.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.060
The necklace the mother wears can also be
seen on the dead grandma as well, so it could

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.430
be a symbol for the hereditary passing down
of traits -- just as biological genes are

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.810
passed down, the tradition of the necklace
could also be passed down.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.939
What I couldn't figure out is what this shape
is supposed to be.

00:03:16.939 --> 00:03:21.010
Let me know your interpretation, but as far
as I can tell, there are three consecutive

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.969
figures, possibly signifying daughter, mother
and grandmother.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:27.079
This next one is just more disturbing when
you think more about it.

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:30.510
Why did this woman make a tiny model of her
own mother on her deathbed?

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.870
I shutter to think of what kind of person
does this.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:39.129
And if that wasn't strange enough, it looks
like the daughter also draws the dead grandma.

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:40.659
This family needs a new hobby.

00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:44.900
And if I'm not mistaken, it looks like the
Grandma's eyes are opening on the other page,

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.859
which is out of focus, which again will be
very unsettling if true.

00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:51.849
Maybe you all picked this up right away, but
this next thing is another one that just got

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:55.530
creepy after I thought about it for a second.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.969
"You know you were always her favorite right?

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:57.969
Even when you were a little baby.

00:03:57.969 --> 00:04:00.139
She wouldn't let me feed you because she needed
to feed you.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.670
Because she needed to feed you.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.390
Because she needed to feed you.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:08.049
Because she needed to feed you."

00:04:08.049 --> 00:04:11.720
Hopefully they were talking about baby formula
but let's face it.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:12.959
It's way too late for that.

00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:15.480
Here are some weird things I noticed about
the daughter.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.970
She's always wearing orange.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.170
She always has these strings tied around her
finger.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.500
And she's got this weird connection with birds.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.480
A bird crashes into her classroom window.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.250
She cuts a bird's head off with scissors.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.530
Totally normal.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.540
She has pictures of birds in her room.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.280
There's also a bird ornament sitting in a
nest in her room.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.290
You could even say her whole room kind of
resembles a bird house.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:38.530
If you think of a birdhouse as a miniature
house that hangs on a tree, so is this.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.160
Speaking of her room, first of all, super
cool.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.890
What kid would not want to live in that?

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.190
But on the inside...

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:49.110
well this guy's just lovely.... and what's
the point of having indoor wind chimes anyway?

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:52.340
I think that's enough of the girl for now...
she's kind of freaky.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.340
Let's move on to the son.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.970
I don't know if it's just me, but he looks
way older than his classmates.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.390
I mean look at this kid.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:04:59.730
Look at her.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.210
Now look at the son.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:05.690
Looks like he got held back a couple times,
but given what happens next I can kind of

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:06.920
see why.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.690
Also there's a poster on the wall behind him
that just says "BIG".

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.920
It could be because everything in this movie
seems to have a miniature version, and if

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.390
the lines between the two do start to blur
at some point as I predicted, there may be

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.360
clues about which world we are in.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:22.230
I think we've established that the kid is
kind of disturbed, so this sign at the school

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.700
that has the words HELP?

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.810
and counselor probably foreshadow a scene
that takes place at said counselor's office

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:28.900
involving the kid.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.111
You may have noticed in this quick shot that
the head from this doll is missing, but what

00:05:33.111 --> 00:05:38.070
you most likely overlooked, is that this is
actually supposed to be the son, Peter.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:42.160
The dresser right here is the same as this
dresser seen in his room, and the position

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.870
of the bed in relation to his desk also matches.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:48.540
The shade of the blue pajamas seems to be
the same as what the doll is wearing and the

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.680
color of the walls and the location of this
stripe all match up.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.830
But of course there had to be inconsistencies
like the missing blinds or the added carpet.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:00.450
I think we can assume that his head smashing
tendencies are probably related to why the

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:05.430
doll has no head, but it also looks like something
is trying to pull his head off just before.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.900
And as promised, there is one major consistency
that could be a big clue as to what's making

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.380
this family so crazy.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:15.300
At the end of the trailer, this flare transitions
the mother's face into the daughter.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:19.370
A similar flair is seen traveling down the
hall at the son's school.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:22.980
I'd love to hear your thoughts about this,
so let me know what you think in the comments.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.410
If you're looking forward to Hereditary, then
leave this video a like.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:31.170
If you're too scared, check out my comedy-horror
web-series The Wokking Dead instead.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:35.690
But regardless of your choice, I'm going to
be covering all the best horror content of

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:41.780
2018, so make sure that you subscribe to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring that deathbell

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:45.320
for notifications and I'll see you in the
next one.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.180
Assuming we both survive.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.120
What?

